# NutNibbles Cursor Rules

NutNibbles is a static personal travel and food journal.

## Priorities
- Premium editorial travel/food magazine feel
- Calm, tasteful, personal, useful
- Strong spacing, clean alignment, good visual rhythm
- Mobile-first and responsive
- No generic AI travel blog tone
- Preserve existing content, links, metadata, sitemap, and static build flow

## Technical rules
- Keep site static HTML/CSS/JS
- Do not add heavy libraries
- Do not rewrite large unrelated sections
- Do not touch unrelated pages unless needed
- Do not commit or push unless explicitly asked
- Always run:
  - npm run build
  - npm run check
  - git diff --check

## Design rules
- Fix layout by improving shared CSS classes first
- Avoid one-off page hacks unless necessary
- Do not judge success only by "no overflow"
- Judge by:
  - visual hierarchy
  - spacing rhythm
  - alignment
  - image proportion
  - mobile readability
  - premium editorial feel

## Current visual concern
The site is functional but still feels too template-like in places.
Focus especially on:
- homepage hero spacing and next-section rhythm
- article hero alignment
- at-a-glance card placement
- pull quote scale
- image/card proportions
- mobile spacing
